{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1408, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an integer array nums.\nYou are allowed to delete any number of elements from nums without making it empty. After performing the deletions, select a subarray of nums such that:\n\nAll elements in the subarray are unique.\nThe sum of the elements in the subarray is maximized.\n\nReturn the maximum sum of such a subarray.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,4,5]\nOutput: 15\nExplanation:\nSelect the entire array without deleting any element to obtain the maximum sum.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [1,1,0,1,1]\nOutput: 1\nExplanation:\nDelete the element nums[0] == 1, nums[1] == 1, nums[2] == 0, and nums[3] == 1. Select the entire array [1] to obtain the maximum sum.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: nums = [1,2,-1,-2,1,0,-1]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation:\nDelete the elements nums[2] == -1 and nums[3] == -2, and select the subarray [2, 1] from [1, 2, 1, 0, -1] to obtain the maximum sum.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= nums.length <= 100\n-100 <= nums[i] <= 100\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def maxSum(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1453, "char_start": 1420, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\nOutput:\n15", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1497, "char_start": 1465, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 1, 0, 1, 1]\nOutput:\n1", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1550, "char_start": 1509, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, -1, -2, 1, 0, -1]\nOutput:\n3", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "e71704461b7cb277993721e1d7a1226c968609a09036399fe6b6d78fa9268d43", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "826a444112b329f659369b9a9aed7a3fb8d9f947867ccf2979d0d3817b1df676", "seq": 2}
